{"ref":"BDB, עִקֵּשׁ","hw":"עִקֵּשׁ","html":"† I. <big><span dir=\"rtl\">עִקֵּשׁ</span></big>  <strong>adj. twisted, perverted</strong>;—abs. <span dir=\"rtl\">דּוֹד ע׳ וּפְתַלְתֹּל</span> <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 32:5\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.32.5\">Dt 32:5</a> <em>a generation twisted and crooked</em>, <span dir=\"rtl\">לֵבָב ע׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 101:4\" href=\"/Psalms.101.4\">ψ 101:4</a>; as n.m. (of one devious in life) <em>the perverted</em> <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 22:27\" href=\"/II_Samuel.22.27\">2 S 22:27</a> = <a data-ref=\"Psalms 18:27\" href=\"/Psalms.18.27\">ψ 18:27</a>, <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 22:5\" href=\"/Proverbs.22.5\">Pr 22:5</a>, of things <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 8:8\" href=\"/Proverbs.8.8\">8:8</a>; cstr. <span dir=\"rtl\">ע׳ דְּרָכַיִם</span> <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 28:6\" href=\"/Proverbs.28.6\">28:6</a>, <span dir=\"rtl\">ע׳ שְׂפָתָיו</span> <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 19:1\" href=\"/Proverbs.19.1\">19:1</a>, <span dir=\"rtl\">עִקֶּשׁ־לֵב</span> <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 17:20\" href=\"/Proverbs.17.20\">17:20</a>; pl. <span dir=\"rtl\">אָרְחֹתֵיהֶם עִקְּשִׁים</span> <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 2:15\" href=\"/Proverbs.2.15\">2:15</a> <em>whose ways are twisted;</em> cstr. <span dir=\"rtl\">עִקְּשֵׁי־לֵב</span> <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 11:20\" href=\"/Proverbs.11.20\">11:20</a>.","next":"BDB, עִקֵּשׁ²","prev":"BDB, עָקַשׁ"}